## DATA MODEL
All data scoped by `userId`. Monthly data uses `month: 'YYYY-MM'`.

| Collection | Shape |
|---|---|
| monthly_income | `{userId, month, income_data}` |
| monthly_expense | `{userId, month, expense_data:[]}` |
| savings | `{userId, month, savings_list:[{savings_type, savings_amount}]}` |
| savingsGoals | `{userId, goalName, targetAmount, status, category, priority, endDate, allocationPercent}` |
| salary | `{userId, month, income, deduct, note}` |
| investment | `{userId, month, investments:[]}` |
| tax_accumulated | `{userId, year, ...}` |
| users | `{userId, username, passwordHash, bankAccounts:[]}` |

savingsGoals `currentAmount` = computed on-the-fly (sum `savings_amount` where `savings_type.toLowerCase() === goalName.toLowerCase()`). Never store in DB.
bankAccounts are stored per-user and exposed via `/api/user-bank-accounts`.

EOM due_day → always pass through `getDueDayNumber()` (dateUtils.js).

## ENV VARS (.env.local)
```
DATA_MODE=mongo
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://user:pass@host1:27017,host2:27017,host3:27017/?authSource=admin&replicaSet=...&tls=true
API_ACCESS_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=...
API_ACCESS_TOKEN_ENCRYPTED=iv:ciphertext
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ACCESS_TOKEN_B64=base64(decryptedToken)  # must match server token exactly
CRON_SECRET=...
LINE_CHANNEL_SECRET=...
```
Token rule: `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_ACCESS_TOKEN_B64` decoded === `API_ACCESS_TOKEN_ENCRYPTED` decrypted → mismatch = `unauthorized`.
MongoDB rule: Use direct `mongodb://`. Never `mongodb+srv://` (Windows DNS blocks SRV lookup).

